   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing an occupancy tax in\nthe village of Weedsport; and providing for the repeal of such provisions upon\nexpiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7493",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7493-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1202-z-2, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7493\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing an occupancy tax\nin the village of Weedsport; and providing for the repeal of such\nprovisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo authorize the village of Weedsport to adopt and amend an occupancy\ntax of up to seven percent\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the tax law to add a new Section 1202-zz to authorize\nthe village of Weedsport to adopt an occupancy tax of up to seven\npercent; define the term hotel; and set fort various miscellaneous\nprovisions.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill is being introduced at the request of the village of Weeds-\nport, in order to provide the village an additional revenue source.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS.8920-A HELMING. Died in Committee\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately, and shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed no more than two years from the date of its enactment.\n",
